{"ticker":"ATKR","generated_at_utc":"2026-10-22T00:29:40.956468Z","profile":{"name":"Atkore Inc.","exchange":"NYSE","country":"United States","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Electrical Equipment & Parts","website":"https://www.atkore.com","summary":"Atkore Inc. engages in the manufacture and sale of electrical, mechanical, safety, and infrastructure products and solutions in the United States and internationally. It operates through two segments, Electrical, and Safety & Infrastructure. The company offers metal electrical conduit and fittings; plastic pipe conduit and fittings; electrical cable and flexible conduit; and international cable management systems; and mechanical tubes and pipes, metal framing and fittings, construction services, perimeter security, and cable management for the protection and reliability of critical infrastructure. It offers its products under the Allied Tube & Conduit, AFC Cable Systems, Kaf-Tech, Heritage Plastics, Unistrut, Power-Strut, Cope, US Tray, FRE Composites, Calbond, and Calpipe. The company serves various end markets, including new construction; maintenance, repair, and remodel; infrastructure; diversified industrials; alternative power generation; healthcare; data centers; and governments. The company was formerly known as Atkore International Group Inc. and changed its name to Atkore Inc. in February 2021. Atkore Inc. was founded in 1959 and is headquartered in Harvey, Illinois."},"stats":{"price":94.96,"marketCap":3207090176.0,"revenueGrowth":0.081,"operatingMargins":0.09663,"fcfMargin":0.10599299845670583,"netCash":-567305024.0,"trailingPE":null,"priceToSales":1.0931765,"beta":1.693,"debtToEquity":0.7158,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":53.75,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":94.97,"avgVolume":967141.0},"bars":[{"d":"2025-10-22","o":67.26,"h":67.48,"l":65.62,"c":66.11,"v":494900},{"d":"2025-10-23","o":66.45,"h":67.93,"l":66.45,"c":67.93,"v":232300},{"d":"2025-10-24","o":68.97,"h":69.35,"l":67.99,"c":68.33,"v":440400},{"d":"2025-10-27","o":68.86,"h"